title: Stage and commit
pid: 8e33c59a-33bc-4803-9232-edeff2dc6e9c
body: |2-
    - Request: =((request . "stage and commit") (message-lines "LINE" ...))=,
      optionally with =(processed-only . t)= or =(confirmed . t)=. MESSAGE,
      the commit message, is its lines joined by newlines; it is sent one
      string per line because the server reads each request up to a
      newline, and its reader does not read =\n= in a string as a newline.
      With =(processed-only . t)= the request commits the processed
      changed nodes of the owned skgrepos, less those that wait for a node
      that does not go in, and asks nothing: =(confirmed . t)= beside it is
      ignored. Without it, it commits every changed node by the same
      commit, asking first unless confirmed. See =docs/diff-view.org=,
      "Stage and commit".
    - Response: LP response-type "stage-and-commit", then a rerender
      stream (rerender-lock, rerender-view*, rerender-done). The
      response is one of:
      - =((needs-confirmation . t) (processed-summary ...) (errors ()) (warnings ()))=
        when the request has neither field and some changed node is not
        processed. The summary has the save response's form, with
        =(notEditable 0)=. Nothing changes, and the rerender stream is
        empty.
      - =((commits (("SKGREPO" "COMMIT-ID") ...)) (committed-nodes N) (left-nodes L) (waiting (("PID" "TITLE" REASON "PID" "TITLE") ...)) (unmarkable (("PID" "TITLE" ("CHANGE" ...)) ...)) (errors (...)) (warnings ()))=
        otherwise. =commits= lists each owned skgrepo git-committed, in
        declaration order, one commit each, by its gitrepo's configured user,
        with MESSAGE; a skgrepo with nothing to commit is not listed. N
        counts the nodes that went in (for a commit of everything, a node
        whose file changed only in bytes the parser does not read
        included); L the changed nodes that did not (=docs/diff-view.org=,
        "The unit is the node"), a container of a merge whose file is
        unchanged among them, and, for a commit of the processed, each
        node whose file changed only in such bytes. Each =waiting= entry
        is a processed node held back, its title, the reason
        (=names-new=, =still-named= or =merge=), and the node it waits for,
        with its title; titles are sent whole, since the connection is
        unrestricted. Each =unmarkable= entry is a node left out because
        one of its files is not what skg writes for it, though every mark
        it can take is set (=docs/diff-view.org=, "Changes no mark
        covers"), its title, and that change, in the user's words: "its
        file changed in a way the diff view does not show (formatting,
        say)". For a commit of everything =waiting=
        and =unmarkable= are empty and L is 0. When nothing is processed,
        or nothing changed, =commits= is empty and N is 0 (for a commit
        of everything, unless some file changed only in bytes the parser
        does not read: that goes in unmarked), e.g.
        =((commits ()) (committed-nodes 0) (left-nodes 5) (waiting ()) (unmarkable ()) (errors ()) (warnings ()))=.
        A commit's tree is HEAD's with the committed nodes' =.skg= files
        taken from the worktree, not the git index; afterwards only those
        paths' git index entries change, to the commit's. An error here
        is a git failure while committing, which stops the rest (N then
        counts only the nodes each of whose files went in; when it is the
        first commit, or some gitrepo's HEAD moved since the commits were
        prepared, =commits= is empty), or a failure after the commits.
        When something was
        committed, the rerender stream rerenders each open buffer of the
        diff view over the rebuilt graph straddle, as any rerender does:
        its roots and what it holds editable stay, and what was committed
        loses its change facts. The marks of the changes committed are
        dropped from the processed store; every other mark stays.
      - =((errors ("REFUSAL")) (warnings ()))= when nothing was
        committed: the connection has a skgrepo restriction, the message
        is blank, the graph straddle cannot be built, an owned gitrepo
        with something to commit has no configured author, or the check
        made before any commit fails ("Nothing was committed: ...").
        The rerender stream is empty.
    - Logic: =server/serve/handlers/stage_and_commit.rs=,
      =server/git_ops/stage_and_commit.rs=, and the choice of nodes in
      =server/diff_view/change_leaves.rs=.
